{{mobile general-purpose computer (non-PC) |brand=Alcatel |model=One Touch 6012A |revision= |upc= |ean= |asin= |price= |est_release_date= |fcc_date=09/03/2013 |manuf_country=China |is_manuf=No |manuf=TCL Corporation |manuf_model= |manuf_rev= |availability= |fcc_id=RAD390 |ic_id= |pwr_v=5 |pwr_amp=0.55 |pwr_conn=USB Female Micro-B |pwr_barrel_outer= |pwr_barrel_inner= |pwr_barrel_len= |pwr_vac= |pwr_ac_hz= |pwr_pol= |pwr_bat_type=Li-Poly |pwr_bat_v=3.8 |pwr_bat_mAh=1700 |pwr_bat_cells= |cpu1_brand=MediaTek |cpu1_model=MT6572A |cpu1_cspeed= |cpu2_brand= |cpu2_model= |cpu2_cspeed= |fla1= |fla1_brand= |fla1_model= |fla1_num= |fla2= |fla2_brand= |fla2_model= |fla2_num= |ram1= |ram1_brand= |ram1_model= |ram1_num= |ram2= |ram2_brand= |ram2_model= |ram2_num= |expansion_if_types=microSD |expansion_pcmcia_num= |expansion_expresscard_num= |expansion_minipci_num= |expansion_minipcie_num= |expansion_usb_num= |jtag= |serial= |wi1_module= |wi1_module_if= |wi1_chip1_brand=MediaTek |wi1_chip1_model= |wi1_chip2_brand= |wi1_chip2_model= |wi1_chip3_brand= |wi1_chip3_model= |ant_conn= |802dot11_protocols=bgn |txchains=1 |rxchains=1 |sstreams=1 |addl_chips= |category=smartphone |stock_os=Android |stock_os_ver= |flags=front-facing camera, rear-facing camera, GPS |oui= }} Per the FCC photos... *This device appears to be using MT6572A. *The battery shown is a ('''Alcatel''' ONETOUCH branded) '''BYD Lithium Battery Co., Ltd.''' TLp017A1 (Li-Poly, 3.8V, 1700mAh / 6.44Wh, made in China) or '''SCUD Co., Ltd.''' TLp017A2 (Li-Poly, 3.8V, 1700mAh / 6.44Wh, made in China, manuf. date shown as 2013-06-06). *The charger (USB, female A connector) shown is an '''Alcatel''' branded S004ACU0500055 (P/N: CBA3007AG0C2, 100-240VAC ~ 50/60Hz, 150mA -> 5VDC, 550mA).
This device may be using a MT6628 Wi-Fi + BT + GPS chip.
{{WiFiCert|WFA20575|07/30/2013}}
